message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - name: "Future AGI"
    website: "https://futureagi.com"
title: "Future AGI"
# Keep these fields aligned with the release manifest and changelog.
# release-please refreshes both when preparing a release; do not pin them manually.
version: 1.56.1 # x-release-please-version
date-released: 2026-10-28 # x-release-please-date
# See LICENSE and LICENSE-EE for the repository's dual licensing terms.
repository-code: "https://github.com/future-agi/future-agi"
keywords:
  - "AI agents"
  - "self-improving agents"
  - "agent evaluation"
  - "agent simulation"
  - "LLM observability"
  - "OpenTelemetry"
  - "guardrails"
  - "LLM gateway"
abstract: >-
  Future AGI is open-source infrastructure for self-improving AI agents. It traces
  and evaluates agent runs, tests agents against simulated users and scenarios,
  and uses the results to optimize prompts, so each round of runs is used to
  improve the agent. It also includes guardrails and an OpenAI-compatible model
  gateway, and can be self-hosted.
